{"seq": 69, "t": 112.12, "ts": "2026-10-30T06:07:18.805668", "run_id": "20261030-060526-66f1", "kind": "preliminary", "agent": "Reporter", "headline": "1,328 of 7,003 delivered orders placed March 2018 were late (19.0%), against 5.6% for a normal baseline. Main causes: carrier transit got slower (72.7% of the rise) and promised delivery windows got shorter (26.7% of the rise).", "summary": "- **What happened:** 1,328 of 7,003 delivered orders placed March 2018 were late (19.0%), against 5.6% for a normal baseline. [T1.A1] The 1,328 late orders were worth R$ 187,138 (order value), with R$ 35,034 of freight paid on them. Their customers gave them 2.1 stars on average, against 4.2 for the orders that arrived on time; 68.3% of their reviews were 1 or 2 stars, against 10.7%. [T2.A1][T2.A2]\n- **Why:** Carrier transit got slower (72.7% of the rise) and promised delivery windows got shorter (26.7% of the rise). Ruled out: Carnival holiday 2018; Severe storm in Rio de Janeiro city; Correios workers' national strike over health plan.\n- **What to do:** A2. Get transit back to normal in SP, RJ, MG (593 orders; R$ 83,603 of orders at stake, 415 with a 1- or 2-star review; within limits). A1. Add delivery-promise buffers where transit outruns the promise (255 orders; R$ 37,740 of orders at stake, 150 with a 1- or 2-star review; needs approval).", "seconds": 12.2, "actions": 2, "unverified": []}
